<title>UK: POLL-Extel analysts survey 1997 rankings - Europe.</title>
<headline>POLL-Extel analysts survey 1997 rankings - Europe.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are results for European economics and strategy research in the 1997 Extel survey rankings of investment analysts, weighted by size of funds managed by the firms which voted for them.</p>
<p>Pan-European economics	 Pan-European equity strategy</p>
<p>1. HSBC James Capel	    1. SBC Warburg</p>
<p>2. Morgan Stanley		2. Morgan Stanley</p>
<p>3. Merrill Lynch		 3. Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>4. Goldman Sachs		 4. Dresdner Kleinwort Benson</p>
<p>5. SBC Warburg		   5. UBS Limited</p>
<p>Countries -- Austria			    Belgium</p>
<p>1. Dresdner Kleinwort Benson 1. Dillon Read Securities 2. SBC Warburg		   2. Petercam</p>
<p>3. HSBC James Capel	    3. Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>Denmark			    Finland</p>
<p>1. Alfred Berg		   1. Alfred Berg</p>
<p>2. FIBA Nordic Securities    2. Enskilda Research</p>
<p>3. Cazenove &amp; Co		 3. FIBA Nordic Securities</p>
<p>France			     Germany</p>
<p>1. Cheuvreux de Virieu	 1. Deutsch Morgan Grenfell</p>
<p>2. SBC Warburg		   2. Dresdner Kleinwort Benson</p>
<p>3. Societe Generale	    3. UBS Limited</p>
<p>Italy				Netherlands</p>
<p>1. SBC Warburg		   1. Labouchere</p>
<p>2. Schroders		     2. HSBC James Capel</p>
<p>3. NatWest Securities	  3. SBC Warburg</p>
<p>Norway			     Spain</p>
<p>1. Alfred Berg		   1. Schroders</p>
<p>2. Enskilda Research	   2. Dillon, Read Securities</p>
<p>3. Den Norske Bank	     3. HSBC James Capel</p>
<p>Sweden			     Switzerland</p>
<p>1. Alfred Berg		   1. Pictet &amp; Cie</p>
<p>2. Enskilda Research	   2. UBS Limited</p>
<p>3. FIBA Nordic Securities    3. SBC Warburg</p>
<p>-- James Saft, London newsroom +171 542 2734</p>
